libkdtree 0.5.0
===============

Incompatible changes
--------------------

- The library version is 1:0:0, so shared builds have the soname
  libkdtree.so.1. Programs built against 0.4.3 must be rebuilt.
- kdtree.h declares only the public API. Internal functions such as
  kd_doBuildTree, kd_allocNode and the heap helpers are no longer
  declared there, and most are no longer exported. kd_freeNode and
  pqueue.h are gone.
- kdtree.h no longer includes pthread.h and string.h. Programs that
  relied on it must include them themselves.
- kd_destroyTree must be given the root of a tree. A tree is two
  blocks of memory, so a subtree can no longer be freed on its own.
- kd_buildTree and kd_sph_buildTree return NULL for a NaN coordinate,
  a NaN corner of the bounding box, a NULL min or max, or a constr
  that returns NULL for non-NULL data. A failing constr used to leave
  NULL data in the tree.

New
---

- pqfree() frees a result queue and the items still in it.

Fixes
-----

- Spherical distances no longer turn into NaN for identical or
  antipodal points, so searches no longer drop exact matches.
- Spherical searches near RA = 0 find all points (GitHub issue #1).
- Building with several threads no longer races in the sort.
- An empty point list returns NULL instead of crashing.
- Failed allocations during building and searching, and failed
  thread creation during building, are handled instead of ignored.
- pqinit(q, 0) no longer overflows on the first insert.
- A failed search no longer frees an uninitialized pointer.

Performance
-----------

- Trees are built with quickselect instead of sorting every level.
  A million random 2-d points build about six times faster.
- A tree takes two allocations instead of about three per node.

Documentation
-------------

- The reference documentation is expanded, with nearest-neighbor
  examples, and published at https://joergdietrich.github.io/libkdtree/
